<title>ISRAEL: Israel forex reserves rose sharply in January.</title>
<headline>Israel forex reserves rose sharply in January.</headline>
<dateline>JERUSALEM 1997-02-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's foreign currency reserves rose by a sharp $1.372 billion to a record $12.792 billion at the end of January, the Bank of Israel said on Sunday.</p>
<p>		    (in millions of dollars)</p>
<p>		  Jan 97    Dec 96    Jan 96</p>
<p>Reserves	12,792    11,464     9,039</p>
<p>The central bank attributed the rise to overseas borrowing by the Israeli government and big purchases of foreign currency by the bank to defend the shekel exchange rate.</p>
<p>- Jerusalem newsroom, 972-2-537-0502</p>
</text>
